            <div xml:id="d856">

                <pb facs="1210" n="1190" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/11–1950: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Drumright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-11-19T16:00:00+09:00">November 19,
                            1950—4 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 19—7:52 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>408. There continued yesterday to be virtually no contact between UN and CCF
                    forces in North Korea (Embtel 398, November 18).</p>
                <p>2. Chinese were taken prisoners yesterday by US 24th Division but affiliation not
                    yet established. Some vehicular traffic, but not of unusual intensity, was noted
                    behind enemy lines, particularly on roads leading north from Onjong. There was
                    no hostile air activity yesterday over North Korea. However, this morning about
                    5:30 local time single hostile aircraft strafed Sunchon area and dropped three
                    bombs.</p>
                <pb facs="1211" n="1191" xml:id="pg1191"/>
                <p>[3.] Numerous reports being received Chinese preparing defensive positions on
                    line running from coast north of Chongju to Taechon, thence to Unsan and thence
                    Northeast to point east of Huichon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Drumright</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
